# ToggleDarkMode

A lightweight tray tool to quickly switch between Windows dark and light mode.

## Why I built this tool

The default way to switch between dark and light mode in Windows usually takes several steps:

`Open Settings -> Personalization -> Colors -> Choose your mode -> Dark / Light -> Close Settings`

This flow is common in daily use but involves too many clicks and is inefficient.  
That's why I built **ToggleDarkMode**:  
Once it's running in the system tray, you can switch the system colour mode with a single click or double-click on the notification area icon.

## Core Features

- One-click toggle between dark and light mode (supports single-click or double-click trigger)
- Quick controls via the tray icon right-click menu
- Toggleable overlay animation when switching
- Adjustable overlay duration (multiple levels)
- Optional launch at startup (can be set during installation or toggled anytime from the program menu)
- Multi-language menu (English / 简体中文 / 繁體中文)
- Single-instance enforcement (prevents multiple tray icons)

## Download & Installation

1. Download [`ToggleDarkMode_1.0_x86.exe`](dist/ToggleDarkMode_1.0_x86.exe)
2. Double-click to run the installer
3. Follow the installation wizard
4. You can launch the program immediately after installation

## How to Use

1. After starting, the program appears in the system tray (notification area, bottom-right corner of the taskbar)
2. Switch between dark and light mode using your configured trigger (single-click / double-click)
3. Right-click the tray icon to open the menu and adjust:
   - Trigger method (single-click toggle / double-click toggle)
   - Overlay on/off
   - Overlay duration
   - Language
   - Launch at startup

## Compatibility & System Requirements

### Architecture compatibility

- Works on both x64 and x86 (64-bit / 32-bit) Windows systems

- `Windows 10 version 1809 and later` – fully supported
- `All Windows 11 versions` – fully supported
- `Windows 10 version 1803 and earlier` – the program runs, but dark/light theme switching may not take effect because the required registry keys are absent

Target coverage: **All Windows 10 1809+ and all Windows 11, zero extra dependencies.**

## Configuration File Location

- The configuration file is saved in your user Documents folder:  
  `Documents\ToggleDarkMode\ToggleDarkMode.cfg`

Notes:

- The configuration is separated from the installation directory to avoid write permission issues when installed under `Program Files`
- The uninstaller does not forcefully delete this configuration file, so your personal settings are preserved

## Known Notes

- If you experience a visual delay after switching, it's usually caused by the system theme refresh speed and is normal Windows behaviour
- If you have manually disabled related theme items or are using third-party theming tools, the toggle effect may be affected
